{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/414475-cwod-vehicle-combat-stunts-and-maneuver-rules-help","id":414475,"title":"cWoD Vehicle Combat, Stunts and Maneuver Rules Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-21T15:07:18-08:00","id":414475,"title":"cWoD Vehicle Combat, Stunts and Maneuver Rules Help","content":"<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Anyone know of any cWoD Rules for </span></span></span>Vehicle Combat, Stunts and Maneuver Rules<span style=\"color:#141823\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">.<br /> <br /> My Werewolf Pack has decided they are going to be a Garou Biker Girl Vigilante Gang, but I am not finding much on Vehicle Stunts except in <b>W20 pg 275</b>. If you know where to look. Have rules. I would appreciate it. I can't find any in the books I took out of storage and I have a whole library of books for WTA and VTA from 1st-20th. I even have some MTA and other books. <br /> <br /> Yes, I know about Bone Gnawer Subway Surfing is in the Bone Gnawer Tribe Book. <br /> <br /> The Totem they are looking at is the <b>General Lee</b>. <br /> <br /> Your Thoughts would be appreciated. Thanks. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:10:31-08:00","id":414485,"title":"","content":"Ramming people can be found in The Hunter's Hunted II.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T15:16:30-08:00","id":414492,"title":"","content":"Do not have that book. It was on my list. I'll have to get it at Paycheck. Anything else?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T22:07:35-08:00","id":414910,"title":"","content":"There are not a lot of printed rules detailing combat stunts in vehicles that I know of. The few I've seen were usually only as an example of the system itself. If you want to stay true to the rules your best bet is to take a look at the roll examples in the V20 and W20 books where they show examples of ability rolls for most common circumstances. Compare some of them mechanically to what you are trying to do and use their framework. You'd get more from that than trying to find a few obscure and rare maneuvers probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T07:24:18-08:00","id":415106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeleton Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/414475-cwod-vehicle-combat-stunts-and-maneuver-rules-help?p=414910#post414910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are not a lot of printed rules detailing combat stunts in vehicles that I know of. The few I've seen were usually only as an example of the system itself. If you want to stay true to the rules your best bet is to take a look at the roll examples in the V20 and W20 books where they show examples of ability rolls for most common circumstances. Compare some of them mechanically to what you are trying to do and use their framework. You'd get more from that than trying to find a few obscure and rare maneuvers probably.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Bah I'll adapt. I am even looking for home rules as well. I am taking out some old non WoD games like TMNT's Road Hogs and trying to adapt them over as well. So far I have found rules on Ramming in Hunters Hunted II and in my Tales of Dark Magick, the Duke and more Motorcycle stats. <br /> <br /> It is easy to convert over even if I have to use nWoD rules to switch over. I want to see if there are any to compile or build from ground up. If there was something in a book I had not cracked open from my books in storage, I wanted to know. <br /> <br /> I know Vehicle stuff has never really been covered in any of the books not even Mage, Surprising since the Technocracy and Traditions you can see a lot of car chases and such there. <br /> <br /> There are only some slight changes really in the end between 1st through 20th Anniversary. <br /> <br /> But thanks any help people are putting here is helping. And if I find them workable and reasonable I'll pass them on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T07:32:17-08:00","id":415110,"title":"","content":"Not quite either WoD rules but <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/103359/Shards-of-the-Exalted-Dream?term=Exalted+shards\" target=\"_blank\">Shards of Exalted Dream</a> has rules for car chases and such can't remember exact details but at least it's a lot more than any WoD book that I remember has. And in the end the rules aren't that different so it shouldn't need much conversion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T08:36:28-08:00","id":415179,"title":"","content":"You know I wonder if Scion might have some rules Possessed that cover this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:41:55-08:00","id":415327,"title":"","content":"NWoD Midnight Roads has a lot of vehicle/travel stuff. It might be relevant.<br /> <br /> Scion has pretty much nada for car chases. Cars are more things to be picked up and used to bash on monsters with. Or to be outrun just for grins and giggles. I ended up having to borrow heavily from the House Rules of others and generate more than a few of my own for my &quot;driver&quot; gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T18:59:41-08:00","id":415967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/414475-cwod-vehicle-combat-stunts-and-maneuver-rules-help?p=415327#post415327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NWoD Midnight Roads has a lot of vehicle/travel stuff. It might be relevant.<br /> <br /> Scion has pretty much nada for car chases. Cars are more things to be picked up and used to bash on monsters with. Or to be outrun just for grins and giggles. I ended up having to borrow heavily from the House Rules of others and generate more than a few of my own for my &quot;driver&quot; gods.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now I am hitting my head on my stupidity. I knew there were rules on what I was looking for. It was in my nWoD book. Gah. Armory has the vehicles. All easy conversions too. Ajax you saved me a lot of time and the Midnight Roads, I got it as a gift never read it. Now this is perfect even for a W20 game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:04:12-08:00","id":416591,"title":"","content":"You're welcome. I am hitting myself on the head for not remembering Armory.<br /> <br /> You might also find something in Adventure, et al. as well. I can't remember, though I need to look at Adventure pretty soon to get the price list in terms of Resources dots for my upcoming 1920's Mage game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T04:37:25-08:00","id":417429,"title":"","content":"If you are looking in nWoD sources; there was that Iron Masters pack, the Lodge of 66, from Lodges the Splintered. It had Rumble of Coming Thunder as the pack totem. Might be something you can use in your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T05:19:40-08:00","id":417449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/414475-cwod-vehicle-combat-stunts-and-maneuver-rules-help?p=417429#post417429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are looking in nWoD sources; there was that Iron Masters pack, the Lodge of 66, from Lodges the Splintered. It had Rumble of Coming Thunder as the pack totem. Might be something you can use in your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry not that familiar with Forsaken. I have the Main Book and Hunting Grounds: Rockies and the Translation Guide that is it in the books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T06:22:23-08:00","id":417475,"title":"","content":"I'm not either truthfully, I just happened to read through that book a couple of times before and your topic sparked a memory of that Lodge. Basically they are like a Pan-tribal Urban Camp of Biker Garou that pay homage to a powerful spirit of the road, &quot;Rumble of Coming Thunder&quot;. The bonus of being associated with the lodge is that they have a vast network of mechanics that grant their members a +1 on all crafts rolls for repairs and modifications to their rides.<br /> <br /> Based on your theme I just thought that the concept might be useful to you as a friend or maybe adversary to your PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T07:02:19-08:00","id":417498,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/414475-cwod-vehicle-combat-stunts-and-maneuver-rules-help?p=417475#post417475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not either truthfully, I just happened to read through that book a couple of times before and your topic sparked a memory of that Lodge. Basically they are like a Pan-tribal Urban Camp of Biker Garou that pay homage to a powerful spirit of the road, &quot;Rumble of Coming Thunder&quot;. The bonus of being associated with the lodge is that they have a vast network of mechanics that grant their members a +1 on all crafts rolls for repairs and modifications to their rides.<br /> <br /> Based on your theme I just thought that the concept might be useful to you as a friend or maybe adversary to your PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not a bad idea, but my Pack is looking right now at the <b>General Lee </b>from the Bone Gnawer Tribe Book, we are modifying it for motorcycles and giving it the name <b>Easy Rider</b>. I am still working on my modifications to this Totem but as <b>General Lee</b> stands it is this. I am modifying this to the idea of the <b>Easy Rider </b>which is designed for Motorcycle packs. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#232323\"><span style=\"font-family:Open Sans\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>General Lee</b>, Background Cost: 5<br /> <br /> While Civil War heroes are certainly very interesting, this great spirit has nothing to do with the War between the States. The General Lee is actually an automotive totem, deriving its name from one of the most famous white trash vehicles ever: The orange muscle car featured on the Dukes of Hazzard. Followers of this totem quest for the car of their dreams, one that they can worship far more than any animal spirit or urban Incarna. After dedicating themselves to \u201cthe General,\u201d the pack hunts to find a neglected, rusting hulk of a car. Typically, a Garou in the pack begins slaving over this monumental gift to at least get the deathtrap running. Some Garou especially Bone Gnawers or Glass Walkers transform these cars into shrines to the totem, often by propping them up on cement blocks in their front yards. With the help of their pack totem, it\u2019s gradually transformed into a paragon of automotive excellence. There\u2019s a reason for this: The car serves as a temperamental totem-spirit, one that can\u2019t enter the spirit world, but can still serve as reliable transportation.<br /> As the pack\u2019s Theurge advances in rank, the lemon is gradually transformed. A Fostern (Rank 2) can actually drive his \u201ctotem car\u201d around, although it\u2019s still a sputtering heap held together by spit and bailing wire. Adren drive masterworks of automotive engineering with whisper quiet engines; reduce all Driving rolls for the car by 1. An Athor\u2019s car never runs out of gasoline, while an elder can actually drive her car into the Umbra. If the car is actually destroyed, its spirit \u201cslumbers in the Umbra\u201d for a full cycle of the moon, then returns to a new set of wheels (and the rusting chassis attached to them) chosen by the pack. Most worshippers of the General can be identified by the wrenches in their back pockets, oil stains on their clothing, or the thunderous sound of their stock cars tearing through the streets.<br /> <b>Individual Traits:</b> Once accepted by the General, everyone in the pack gets an additional two dots of Drive and two dots of Crafts (if this would grant them a specialty, they automatically get the Repair specialty). All pack members have the difficulty of any Drive rolls related to tricky or dangerous maneuvers reduced by 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Traits:</b> The pack alpha gains an intuitive knowledge of all of America\u2019s highways, along with many back roads in the Deep South.<br /> <br /> <b>Ban:</b> Worshippers of the General endlessly tinker with their cars. As part of this, at least one member of the pack must have mechanic\u2019s tools ready at all times. There\u2019s a good reason for this: The pack\u2019s totem spirit lives in the car they care for. Tinkering with the pack\u2019s chosen car gives spiritual strength to the totem spirit. For all practical intents and purposes, the totem spirit is bound to the car, and it can only go where the car goes. Each day, a member of the pack must spend at least an hour making repairs, improvements, and modifications to this shrine. If the pack skips a day, the car begins to degrade, gaining one temporary fault. Each day, someone in the pack can attempt a Wits + Repair roll (difficulty 6) to fix this. This is a sizeable ban, but it has its benefits as well. After years of reverent worship, these vehicles can reach a peak performance of mythical proportions. With a capable driver behind the wheel, some are capable of performing stunts rarely seen outside of \u201970s car chases. As part of this, when the driver is Rank Three or higher, anytime he fails a driving check, the totem spirit can then attempt a second roll using its Willpower as a Dexterity + Driving dice pool.</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T11:48:12-08:00","id":417748,"title":"","content":"Yeah I am familiar with that Totem, played a pack member who was under the General for awhile during a &quot;Fast &amp; Furious&quot; like Chronicle lol. I really like your idea, good name! What kind of mods are you making, if you don't mind me asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:35:13-08:00","id":417900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/414475-cwod-vehicle-combat-stunts-and-maneuver-rules-help?p=417748#post417748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I am familiar with that Totem, played a pack member who was under the General for awhile during a &quot;Fast &amp; Furious&quot; like Chronicle lol. I really like your idea, good name! What kind of mods are you making, if you don't mind me asking?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have not gotten there yet. I just finished converting the Motorcycles from 3 Different WoD sources to W20. When I make the changes and such I will add it here. I have to finish a One Shot to I am running for charity and because I work in helping the poor this is actually work. The local gaming community is doing a fund raiser for the local food bank here in Albuquerque, NM at Active Imagination this Saturday. I am running a One Shot Hengeyokai game in Tokyo using the Changing Breeds book and Hengeyokai. from 4 pm- 8 pm. The Whole Event is Noon to Midnight. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}